message:
I am thinking...: The crash is a heap-double-free in `hb_vector_t<CFF::op_str_t, 8u>::fini` called from `hb_vector_t<CFF::cff1_font_dict_values_t, 8u>::~hb_vector_t`, which is called from `OT::cff1::accelerator_templ_t<CFF::cff1_private_dict_opset_t, CFF::cff1_private_>`.

Looking at the `fini` method (line ~1155):
```cpp
inline void fini (void)
{
  sc.end_processing ();
  topDict.fini ();
  fontDicts.fini_deep ();
  privateDicts.fini_deep ();
  hb_blob_destroy (blob);
  blob = nullptr;
}
```

The issue is in the `init` method. When `privateDicts.resize(fdCount)` is called and then `privateDicts[i].init()` is called in a loop, if any failure happens later (e.g., during font dict parsing), the `fini()` method will call `privateDicts.fini_deep()` which will call `fini()` on each element. But then, when parsing font dicts, `fontDicts.push()` is called to add new elements. If the push fails or some other error occurs, `fini()` is called which does `fontDicts.fini_deep()`.

The issue seems to be that `fontDicts` elements contain `op_str_t` vectors. When a font dict is interpreted and then fini is called, the `op_str_t` elements inside could be double-freed.

Wait, let me look more carefully at the crash state:
- `hb_vector_t<CFF::op_str_t, 8u>::fini`
- `hb_vector_t<CFF::cff1_font_dict_values_t, 8u>::~hb_vector_t`

So the double-free happens when destroying the fontDicts vector. Each `cff1_font_dict_values_t` contains an `op_str_t` vector that gets double-freed.

Let me look at the `hb_vector_t` class to understand why a double-free could occur.

